From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:20:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/44] minimize: window items share the space before they
 overflow

Items were 180 px, and the count assumed icon-sized slots and kept at least
two. The applet then grew or shrank by a whole item, more than the panel's
84 px of slack, so the panel kept shrinking and relaxing it: the taskbar
flickered between all items and the overflow button and drew over the tray.

Items now stay at their full width while they fit, else share the space down
to a minimum; only then do the rest go to the overflow popup, whose button
gets its room. A limited space is filled to within a few pixels, so the size
is stable. The overflow popup lists its windows as the same items, one below
the other. The widths (180, 120 and 300 px) can be changed in
~/.config/minimize-ws/sizes.

